course: dictionary
lesson: 12623
title: Disloyalty: not standing by someone
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Disloyalty is a noun. It means not being loyal, which is failing to stand by or be faithful to someone. You can be disloyal to a friend, a family, a team, a country or a cause. Inside the word is loyal, which means faithful and true, so disloyalty is its opposite.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «Telling your best friend's secret was an act of disloyalty.» A secret is private, and your friend trusted you to keep it. So disloyalty means letting someone down when they are counting on you.
explain: Disloyalty can also mean one single action. «An act of disloyalty» is one thing done that is not loyal. The plural, disloyalties, means more than one such act. Ask yourself: who is being let down? That tells you what the disloyalty is to.
fact: Disloyalty is a noun. It means not being loyal.
fact: «Loyal» means faithful and true to a friend, family, team, country or cause.
fact: «Disloyalty to» is followed by the person or thing you let down, as in «disloyalty to a friend».
fact: «Accused of disloyalty» means someone says you were not loyal, even if you do not agree.
fact: In the Bible, Judas' betrayal and Peter's denial are famous stories of disloyalty, and Peter was forgiven.
exercise: «Telling a friend's secret is an act of disloyalty.» What does disloyalty mean here? | *Not being faithful to a friend | Sharing a happy surprise | Shouting loudly at a friend | Keeping a friend safe
exercise: «The soldier was accused of disloyalty to his king.» What does accused of disloyalty mean? | Asked to go home for lunch | Thanked for being very brave | Given a medal by the king | *Blamed for not being faithful to the king
exercise: Which word is the opposite of disloyalty? | Laughter | Anger | Silence | *Loyalty
test: «Ella said two acts of disloyalty had hurt her.» Which word shows more than one act? | Loyal | Disloyalty | *Disloyalties | Disloyal
test: In the Bible, Peter denied knowing Jesus, but he was forgiven. What is Peter's story an example of? | Kindness | *Disloyalty | Loyalty | Courage
exam: «Ben kept his friend's secret, even when it was hard.» What did Ben show? | Anger | *Loyalty | Disloyalty | Boredom
